    "text": "Ailbe, also called Ailba, was a famous hunting dog in Irish myth. The warrior Mac Dathó owned him. Two powerful provincial kings each wanted the dog, and Mac Dathó wished to satisfy both. He promised Ailbe to Concobar Mac Nessa of Ulster and to Ailill Mac Mata of Connacht. The argument that followed ended with the dog killed.",
